### Smoke Test Flow (End-to-End Sanity Check)

### 1. Create Author User
# @name smokeCreateUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "SmokeTest",
  "lastName": "User",
  "email": "smoketest.user@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

###

### 2. Create Tag
# @name smokeCreateTag
POST {{baseUrl}}/tags
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "smoke-test-tag",
  "slug": "smoke-test-tag",
  "description": "Tag generated during E2E smoke test"
}

###

### 3. Create Post (Chained with created user ID & tag ID)
# @name smokeCreatePost
POST {{baseUrl}}/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Smoke Test Post",
  "postType": "post",
  "slug": "smoke-test-post",
  "status": "published",
  "content": "This post was created during the end-to-end smoke test execution.",
  "authorId": {{smokeCreateUser.response.body.$.id}},
  "tags": [{{smokeCreateTag.response.body.$.id}}]
}

###

### 4. Fetch All Posts (Verify post creation & relations)
GET {{baseUrl}}/posts
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 5. Cleanup: Delete Created Post
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/posts/{{smokeCreatePost.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 6. Cleanup: Soft Delete Tag
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tags/{{smokeCreateTag.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
